.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.DS_Store
data/cache/*
!data/cache/.gitkeep
# Every tracking-database file, whatever it is called. These used to be three
# literal `data/tracking.db*` lines, which covered the one name in active use
# and nothing else -- so `data/tracking 2.db-shm` and `data/tracking 3.db-wal`
# (copies a developer made on a machine where the path has a space in it) were
# tracked in git, WAL journals included. Tracked too, a reviewer reads them as
# data: a WAL is a pending-transaction log, and what it contains depends on
# whoever last opened the database. Ignoring is strictly safer than deleting --
# a local copy stays on disk for whoever made it.
data/tracking*.db
data/tracking*.db-shm
data/tracking*.db-wal
data/*.db
data/*.db-shm
data/*.db-wal
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.worktrees/
.claude/worktrees/

# Regenerable diagnostics from `evaluate/scoreline_selection.py`. Deliberately
# not tracked: `models/manifest.json` embeds its content, so this file is only a
# transport. Committing it would let a stale copy ship as though it were current
# -- and a stale headline is worse than an absent one, which is why a retrain on
# a fresh checkout reports `walk_forward_status: not_computed` rather than
# inventing a figure.
models/selection_walk_forward.json
